If $H nsub G$, then $g h g^(-1) in H$ gives $g h = (g h g^(-1)) g in H g$ for every $h in H$, so $g H subset.eq H g$. Applying the same argument to $g^(-1)$ gives $H g subset.eq g H$, hence $g H = H g$.

Conversely, if $g H = H g$ for every $g in G$, then $g h in H g$ for $h in H$, so $g h = h' g$ for some $h' in H$. Therefore $g h g^(-1) = h' in H$, and $H nsub G$.
